Progress — first test passes now. The rerace test fails at "failed race must clear lastGood": after the failed race, `lastGood["beta"].Addr` is still set.

Look at Tick's racing loop:

```go
won := false
for _, cand := range p.ordered { ... if tryConnect → won=true ... }
if !won && !p.haveWin {
    dm.lastGood[p.name] = Candidate{}
}
```

In this scenario: first tick succeeded → lastGood["beta"] = hostC(lanPeer). Second tick: p.haveWin = true (from lastGood), freshNow forced stale, Reachable=false so no handshake. Racing: ordered has 1 candidate (host lanPeer). pickInitial already... in the racing loop we iterate ALL ordered candidates including the previous winner. tryConnect fails (Reachable false). won=false. Condition `!won && !p.haveWin` → haveWin is TRUE → doesn't clear.

Bug: the clear condition should be just `!won`. But careful: if a peer previously converged and this tick's race fails transiently, clearing lastGood means next tick re-races from scratch — which is correct behavior for a dead path.

But there's a subtlety: `!won && !p.haveWin` was maybe intended to preserve winner when candidates list empty? No — empty ordered skips loop, won=false, and we'd clear a still-plausible winner on a roster blip. Better: only clear when we actually attempted (len(ordered)>0):

```go
if !won && len(p.ordered) > 0 {
    dm.lastGood[p.name] = Candidate{}
}

